WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.360
Close your eyes. A vibrator on your biceps tendon, at 100 Hertz can make you

2
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.360
misjudge where your elbow is.

3
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.160
The joint has not moved.

4
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:19.300
In one classic experiment on human subjects, the error reached as much as 40 degrees

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.660
while the muscle contracted.

6
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.020
So your sense of limb position is a computed estimate, built from sensors you cannot

7
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.020
feel.

8
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.480
Position is read from populations of afferents, not from one receptor.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.160
Take the muscle spindle.

10
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:39.540
It has one primary ending, called Ia, and usually one or more secondary endings,

11
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.280
called type II. Both signal static muscle length.

12
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.240
Ia endings are also more sensitive to the rate of change.

13
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:53.200
So the old rule, that Ia is velocity and type II is position, is wrong.

14
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:56.963
Human recordings separate the two classes by vibration.

15
00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:03.043
In the leg of healthy people, one study recorded 15 primary and 5 secondary endings.

16
00:01:03.703 --> 00:01:07.943
The secondary endings were less sensitive to low -amplitude tendon vibration.

17
00:01:08.543 --> 00:01:11.723
So primary endings are the likely carriers of the illusion.

18
00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:14.743
But the experiments do not show that only they act.

19
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:19.437
Which protein turns stretch into current at a spindle ending?

20
00:01:19.957 --> 00:01:22.137
A channel called piezo -2?

21
00:01:22.677 --> 00:01:25.437
In mouse, three kinds of evidence were gathered.

22
00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:27.337
First, where it is.

23
00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:31.037
A reporter showed it in endings on spindles and tendon organs.

24
00:01:31.637 --> 00:01:33.457
Second, what current it carries.

25
00:01:34.137 --> 00:01:37.517
Dissociated sensory neurons gave rapidly adapting currents.

26
00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.217
Third, whether the ending needs it.

27
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:43.237
Deleting it sharply reduced stretch of oaked firing.

28
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:50.437
In mouse cell bodies and culture, 23 of 25 labelled neurons had rapidly adapting

29
00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:54.637
currents. The label marks proprioceptors and some other neurons.

30
00:01:55.197 --> 00:01:59.137
The inactivation time constant was 5 .6 milliseconds.

31
00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:01.957
Assume one exponential decay.

32
00:02:02.597 --> 00:02:04.977
That is our assumption, not the paper's.

33
00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:10.317
About 17% % is left at 10 milliseconds and about 3% % at 20

34
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:15.970
A small stretch response remained after deletion, in one of eight muscles for each

35
00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:22.010
mouse line. So Piezo2 is the principal transducer; the residue does not prove

36
00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:27.830
another channel. In humans, two people with inactivating PIEZO2 variants were

37
00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.210
markedly worse at reaching and joint angle tasks without visual cues.

38
00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.610
Two people are a clinical series.

39
00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.810
Keep this rule. Limb position is an estimate from many signals.
